# Opinion

Meeting: 0002-bootstrap-rps-arena-platform
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: bootstrap RPS Arena platform
Context:
- New standalone “RPS Arena” project using Node/HTML5 with classic/extreme modes, ranked/casual queues, unlockables, and MongoDB as the data store.
- Requirements: avoid heavy dependencies, keep gameplay server-authoritative, ship Azure-ready CI/CD, and maintain full test coverage.

Position:
- Favor a lean, explicit service layer over heavy frameworks: Node HTTP server + small service modules + repository abstraction (in-memory + MongoDB).
- Keep separation of concerns crisp (validation, game logic, matchmaking, persistence, presentation) to keep performance and auditability high.

Recommendations:
- Default to in-memory for dev/local UX, but keep Mongo repository first-class with a single entry point to swap storage without changing services.
- Maintain pure, deterministic game/elo logic modules so we can reason about fairness and add new variants safely.
- Preserve small dependency surface (only mongodb + c8) and continue expressing flows in plain JS modules for portability and ease of review.
